I-sec17.1-electronic-programmable", "claim": "The incident may trigger obligations related to fault tolerance and risk mitigation.", "support_note": "This regulation addresses the need for mitigating risks in case of a single fault condition.", "support_status": "supported"}], "confidence": 0.75, "evidence_links": [{"artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec17.4-it-security", "artifact_type": "regulatory citation", "relevance_note": "Relevant to software security and integrity."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.10-c-design-development", "artifact_type": "regulatory citation", "relevance_note": "Applies design controls to devices with automated software."}, {"artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec17.1-electronic-programmable", "artifact_type": "regulatory citation", "relevance_note": "Addresses fault tolerance and risk mitigation in programmable devices."}, {"artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec17.2-software-lifecycle", "artifact_type": "regulatory citation", "relevance_note": "Mandates a robust software development lifecycle, including risk management and cybersecurity."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Provides device confidence score data related to the missed event. Further analysis of this log may reveal contributing factors."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Provides device confidence score data related to the missed event. Further analysis of this log may reveal contributing factors."}], "missing_evidence": [], "rationale": "The incident narrative describes a non-recurrent ventricular tachycardia-adjacent irregularity detected by synthetic remote monitoring center telemetry. While no adverse patient outcome was recorded, the fact that a clinician note documenting this event was not filed raises concerns about potential recurrence and incomplete recordkeeping. This requires investigation to determine root cause and ensure appropriate documentation practices are in place. The device incorporates software, triggering obligations under EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.2 regarding software development lifecycle and cybersecurity, as well as 21 CFR \u00a7 820.10(c) concerning design controls for devices automated with computer software. Furthermore, the event may trigger obligations under EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.1 requiring appropriate means to eliminate or reduce risks in the event of a single fault condition.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 2}, "final_report_sha256": "0648cc5e3eae5165cfc81ba986d8b8b67ea1bba4ee7e6783f40a3a853d98f29e", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": [], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0020", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 0, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0020_r3", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0020", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 2, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "advisory_complete", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-04T22:44:28.501798Z", "total_steps": 4, "trace_id": "abd60a14-91dc-4e09-8774-6f0b6b1741d5"}
